  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Games Based HIV&amp;AIDS awareness creation in Catholic Diocese of Tombura/Yambio.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a 6 month internal project co-funded by CAFOD and Caritas Australia to be implemented by CAFOD through 3rd party service provider specialising in using sports/games to raise awareness on specific social issues affecting comunities, with focus on HIV&amp;AIDS in this particular case. The project is planned as part of the centenary celebrations of the diocese of Tombura/Yambio, HIV&amp;AIDS has been one of the key topics of discusions during the various church centenary activities and the project is aimed at contributing to the overall 3 year programme using a different methodology to enhance awareness among the communities and church structures at parish and diocesan levels in responding to the fight against HIV&amp;AIDS with the aim of increasing personal and community risk perceptions to reduce and prevent new HIV infections as well as re-infections most especially among the most at risk populations (i.e. youths, teenagers, women, etc). The project targets all the 13 parishes in the diocese of Tombura-Yambio. The project will massively contribute to realising the 3 year overall targeted 25,000+ beneficiaries in the wider programme. The project major components focus on prevention through use of sports awareness campaign initiatives, advocacy, and capacity building of the local structures in diversified use of awareness strategies.</narrative>
  </description>
